This interpretation was based on the identification of the pope as Antichrist, the historic Reformation concept. The principal exponent of this interpretation was Andreas Helwig (c. 1572–1643; see L. E. Froom, The Prophetic Faith of Our Fathers, vol. 2, pp. 605–608). Many since his day have adopted this interpretation. Inasmuch as this commentary identifies the beast as the papacy, it also accepts this view as being the beast thus far presented, though');
INSERT INTO commentaries (author, book, chapter, verse, text) VALUES ('Comentário Bíblico Adventista VII', 'Apocalipse', 13, 0, 'ELLEN G. WHITE COMMENTS
  2 GC 54,  445, 578; SR 331
  2, 3 GC 439
  3 GC 579; 6T 14
  5–7 GC 54, 439; SR 331
  8 AA 229; GC 579; PP 63
  10, 11 GC 439
  11 GC 440; TM 117; 5T 452; 9T 229
  11, 12 GC 441,  442, 578
  11–17 DA 122
  13 EW 59, 87; GC 612
  13, 14 GC 553; SR 395
